\section{Errors and refusals}{
The weight-semantics, positive-weight, \code{igraph} and \code{wave} refusals are the
same ones \code{\link[=compute_centrality]{compute_centrality()}} documents, because both resolve through the
same engine. Two are specific to this function:
\itemize{
\item \strong{A node-level measure with no \code{summary}}, e.g. \code{"degree"}: it has one
value per node and this function returns one row per group, so rnetis asks
which summary you mean rather than picking one. Use
\code{\link[=compute_centrality]{compute_centrality()}} for the node-level values themselves.
\item \strong{\code{summary} supplied for a measure that is already group-level}, e.g.
\code{"density"}: there is nothing to aggregate.
}

\strong{Computing a constant is not refused here.} A single group with one
resolved snapshot gives one density value, which is a perfectly good number
to look at. What is refused — by \code{\link[=fit_influence]{fit_influence()}}, on a \code{\link[=network_stat]{network_stat()}}
term — is \emph{estimating a coefficient} on it, because a constant predictor is
perfectly collinear with the intercept. Inspection and estimation are
different questions, and only the second one is unidentified.
}

